# Quantumult X subscription normalization example
#
# Optional fragment for [server_remote].
# Requires:
# - resource_parser_url configured in [general]
# - opt-parser=true on the subscription
#
# Keep the normal subscription form unless your provider's node tags cannot be
# recognized by this repository's server-tag-regex policies.

# Basic subscription:
# https://YOUR_SUBSCRIPTION_URL, tag=Main Subscription, opt-parser=true, update-interval=86400, enabled=true

# Remove obvious non-node metadata from node names.
# delreg uses a regular expression against the node name.
# https://YOUR_SUBSCRIPTION_URL#delreg=(剩余|套餐|流量|到期|官网|注册|重置), tag=Normalized Subscription, opt-parser=true, update-interval=86400, enabled=true

# Normalize provider-specific city labels into stable region tokens.
# KOP-XIAO resource-parser rename syntax:
#   rename=旧名@新名+旧名@新名+...
#
# Example mappings:
#   洛杉矶 -> US
#   圣何塞 -> US
#   西雅图 -> US
#   东京   -> JP
#   大阪   -> JP
#   新加坡 -> SG
#   伦敦   -> UK
#
# https://YOUR_SUBSCRIPTION_URL#delreg=(剩余|套餐|流量|到期|官网|注册|重置)&rename=洛杉矶@US+圣何塞@US+西雅图@US+东京@JP+大阪@JP+新加坡@SG+伦敦@UK, tag=Normalized Subscription, opt-parser=true, update-interval=86400, enabled=true

# Notes:
# 1. Do not add a mapping unless you know what the provider label means.
# 2. Do not map opaque labels such as "Premium-A" to a country by guesswork.
# 3. AI safe-node routing still validates the real exit region and provider
#    reachability; normalization only helps candidate discovery.
